%% Customer profile, address ownership, and account linking
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Customer
    participant Web as Customer Web/BFF
    participant API as Customer account API
    participant Auth as Authenticated principal
    participant Account as CustomerAccountService
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL

    Customer->>Web: Open account or checkout address manager
    Web->>API: GET profile, customer, and addresses
    API->>Auth: Require authenticated tenant user
    Auth->>Account: Resolve principal-owned customer
    Account->>DB: Read tenant-local user/customer/address rows
    DB-->>Account: Customer projection and addresses
    Account-->>API: Customer projection and addresses
    API-->>Web: Customer projection and addresses

    opt First account-to-customer link
        Customer->>Web: Submit order reference and placement phone
        Web->>API: POST account/customer-link
        API->>Account: Verify exact order and phone proof
        Account->>DB: Check unlinked user/customer and attach atomically
        DB-->>Account: Linked customer account
        Account-->>API: Linked customer account
        API-->>Web: Linked customer account
    end

    Customer->>Web: Create, edit, delete, or set default address
    Web->>API: Address mutation with address ID when applicable
    API->>Auth: Resolve authenticated customer ID
    Auth->>Account: Apply owner-scoped mutation
    Account->>DB: Update only matching tenant + customer address
    Account->>DB: Clear previous default and promote selected address
    DB-->>Account: Updated customer/address projection
    Account-->>API: Updated customer/address projection
    API-->>Web: Updated customer/address projection

    Note over Auth,DB: Raw user, customer, or address IDs are never sufficient without tenant and owner predicates.
    Note over Account,DB: Profile synchronization and default-address invariant are maintained transactionally.
